                    <chunk name="param_input" index="14">
                      <items count="9">
                        <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">How the solver treats the ground (OpenLB, CPU image only). None is the no-slip bounce-back: it lets the log-law inflow collapse in the lowest cells (measured at 1 m cells: -53 % at 1.5 m after 100 m). Power law and Spalding are OpenLB's wall-modelled ground and hold the profile; they are smooth-wall models. Rough adds the rough-wall log law with the ABL's z0, so the ground shear follows the roughness like OpenFOAM's rough wall function. Costs about 2.5x the run time.</item>
                        <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">eb755f43-d4a8-4a97-bdf5-77832ee4a2d4</item>
