                    <chunk name="param_input" index="17">
                      <items count="7">
                        <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Turbulent inflow (OpenLB, CPU image only): OpenLB's vortex method adds random eddies to the log-law inlet, sized ~0.4 x the reference height, with the intensity of the log law (I_u = 1/ln(z/z0)), refreshed once per eddy passage. Replaces Jitter. On AIJ Case A it cut the wake's bias from +0.88 to +0.59 and the reattachment length from 2.0 H to 1.3 H against the steady inflow at H/20, and beat the jitter at both resolutions tried (docs/VALIDATION.md 10b), so it is the default. With GPU on the CUDA image has no vortex method: the run keeps the jitter and says so. Off = the steady profile (the validation control).</item>
                        <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">0830e6dd-02f6-4b69-926c-fbe0ab832956</item>
                        <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Synthetic Turbulence</item>
                        <item name="NickName" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Turb</item>
                        <item name="Optional" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">true</item>
                        <item name="SourceCount" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">0</item>
                        <item name="Value" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">true</item>
                      </items>
                      <chunks count="2">
                        <chunk name="Attributes">
                          <items count="2">
                            <item name="Bounds" type_name="gh_drawing_rectanglef" type_code="35">
