                        <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Time-varying wind (OpenLB), one line or item per point: time (s), wind speed at the ABL's reference height (m/s), wind direction (deg, from, clockwise from north) - e.g. hourly weather replayed in minutes. Linear between points, held beyond the ends; the time-averaged result covers the averaging window. Every direction must stay within 45 degrees of the ABL direction (with Jitter): set the ABL to the mean direction. Empty = a steady wind.</item>
                        <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">f209b572-8fe9-4ea1-a936-e9b6dc5b52c3</item>
