                    <chunk name="param_input" index="15">
                      <items count="9">
                        <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Roof detail. LoD 1.2: one flat roof per footprint (Roof Percentile of its points). LoD 1.3: one flat roof per height level (a tower on a podium is two; a pitched roof stays one). LoD 2.0: ONE standard roof per building — flat, shed, gable or hip, whichever fits its roof points best (flat when within 15 %) — on the footprint's oriented box, clipped to the footprint: the cleanest choice where the LiDAR is sparse or trees overhang. LoD 2.1: roof planes like 2.2, but details from 4 m only: smaller parts are merged (unless they stand 4 m above their neighbours — a shaft is not a detail), and a pitched plane whose points are thinner than 3 m on the map (a wall, an eave line) is dropped. LoD 2.2: roof planes fitted to the roof points (pitched roofs, ridges, steps between levels), details from 2 m. At every 2.x level a footprint with a Height, or without enough points for a plane, stays LoD 1.2.</item>
                        <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">dfeac701-0903-4c96-939a-198d0fca90b3</item>
                        <item name="Multiple" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">false</item>
